ost to the Soviet Union 11-8 and missed out on the final on goal difference. In the other pool, reigning world champion Romania was surprised by Yugoslavia, which moved away from the Romanians in the second half to beat them 14-13 in a low-scoring affair."] "\n\n" [:p {} "This gave Romania vs. East Germany, the World Championship final of 1970, as the bronze medal match in München. Two years earlier, the Romanians required two overtimes to get rid of the Germans, but this time they obtained an early lead, giving them a 19-16 win in the end. The final was slightly disappointing. The Yugoslavs started with a 4-0 lead after six minutes, and protected a seven-point advantage in the first half. This sealed the fate of Czechoslovakia, which never recovered and lost 21-16."] "\n"] [:button {:id "button808798", :class "btn btn-default"} "Details"] [:script {} "$('#button808798').click(splits)"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {}] [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Team"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {:style "display: none", :class "split"} "Games"] [:th {:style "display: none", :class "split"} "Attempts / Shots on Goal"] [:th {:style "display: none", :class "split"} "Attempts / Shots on Goal"] [:th {:style "display: none", :class "split"} "Shots % / Save %"] [:th {:style "display: none", :class "split"} "7 metre Shots / Attempts"] [:th {:style "display: none", :class "split"} "Warnings"] [:th {:style "display: none", :class "split"} "Suspensions"] [:th {:style "display: none", :class "split"} "Disqualifications"] [:th {:style "display: none", :class "split"} "Exclusions"] [:th {:style "display: none", :class "split"} "Wins"] [:th {:style "display: none", :class "split"} "Draws"] [:th {:style "display: none", :class "split"} "Losses"] [:th {:style "display: none", :class "split"} "Points"] [:th {:style "display: none", :class "split"} "Goals"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {:class "accordion-toggle", :da